# The release hands ffiPackagingCheckAll its downloaded pool on the command line, where it is a
# session setting. A command that rebuilds the build from the settings without the session drops it,
# and the check then reads only what this host compiled: every platform a producer supplied reports
# as missing while the natives for it sit unread in the pool.

# This host's own compile is well formed, so the check passes with no pool in play.
> ffiPackagingCheckAll

# The pool holds a malformed artifact for a declared id. Rejecting it is the only outcome available
# to a check that can see the pool, so this failing is what proves the setting arrived.
> set ThisBuild / ffiPrebuiltPool := Some(file("pool"))
-> ffiPackagingCheckAll

# The formats-only command reaches the same pool by the same route.
-> ffiPackagingFormatCheckAll
